      "writtenOn": "2026-08-18T06:22:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The `--ignore-scripts` flag is good for security (prevents malicious install scripts), but consider adding error handling or a follow-up step to verify the installation succeeded. If npm ci fails silently, the audit step will run against an incomplete or empty node_modules.\nConsider adding something like\n```\n - name: Verify installation\n   run: test -d node_modules || exit 1\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 29,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 30,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "4be85c9a3725faf75b752d28f6202327c12a75b1",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
