      "writtenOn": "2026-08-24T06:56:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the suggestion! However, `npm ci` is not silent on failure — it exits with a non-zero status code for any installation error which GitHub Actions already treats as a step failure and halts all subsequent steps immediately. \nSo the `Run npm audit` step is never reached if `npm ci` fails.\n\n\nA `test -d node_modules` check would only be meaningful if `npm ci` could exit `0` while leaving `node_modules` absent — that cannot happen with any released version of npm. \n\nThe check would add a step that unconditionally passes on every single run without providing any additional safety net. So the current workflow is already protected by `npm ci`\u0027s own exit code. No change needed here.",
      "parentUuid": "ac44de55_8bf3ed46",
